<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen firmer, miners to support.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen firmer, miners to support.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 9.00 a.m./2300 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2723.80  +32.60   DJIA  cl	8121.11   +7.67</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2753     +11   US 30yr cl	 6.40   -0.06</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.505  +0.030   Gold NY 328.75 Lon fix 325.75</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7363 (Mon 0.7362)   CRB Index cl   241.18   +2.70</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20575.26 +185.72   FTSE cl	 4862.60  +11.10</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   942.75   -0.90   NZSE40	  2566.18  +24.07</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 29)----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen firmer with stronger gold and firm base metals prices to underpin. &quot;The metals (stocks) should hold our market quite nicely today, up about 10-15 points early,&quot; said a broker.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.30 (-.03), A$19.58 (-.15), A$6.22 (-.01), A$7.90 (+.03)</p>
<p>*Wall Street stocks turned in a mixed performance with the Dow scratching out marginal gains and tech stocks falling ahead of a barrage of economic data.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 18-13/16 (+10/16), BHP 27-1/16 (+8/16), WMC 23-1/8 (+3/16), National Australia Bank 72-13/16 (+1-5/16)</p>
<p>*Gold price was higher, on LME zinc prices marched higher, copper dipped but found support, while nickel forged ahead.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
